answer.worked:
The speed is the magnitude of the rate of change of distance with respect to time (velocity). Differentiate $S$ with respect to $t$:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{dS}{dt} &= 55\,000 \times (-0.182 \ln 3) \times 3^{-0.182t} \\
&= -10\,010 \ln 3 \times 3^{-0.182t}
\end{align*}$$
Substitute $t = 2$ to find the velocity:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{dS}{dt} &= -10\,010 \ln 3 \times 3^{-0.182(2)} \\
&= -10\,010 \ln 3 \times 3^{-0.364} \\
&\approx -7372.3576
\end{align*}$$
Speed is the absolute value of velocity:
$$\begin{align*}
\text{Speed} &\approx 7372.36 \text{ km/h}
\end{align*}$$
The speed of the rocket after 2 hours is approximately $7372 \text{ km/h}$.

